const STANDARDS = `ENGINEERING STANDARDS (non-negotiable)
- Python >= 3.10, full type hints, docstrings on every public class/function, pydantic v2 models for all configs/plans/outputs, async-first with sync wrappers where useful.
- Read these files FIRST and follow them exactly: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md (sections 1-3, 5, 6 and your model's section), common/README.md, and the actual source of common/pipeline_core/*.py (contracts.py, component.py, llm.py, prompts.py, domain.py, protocols.py, telemetry.py, utils.py, errors.py). Use the real signatures; do not guess the core API.
- LLM calls only through ctx.llm_call(LLMRequest(...)) inside plan()/execute(), or through self.llm.complete() in direct-API methods that receive no ctx (then account usage yourself). Stable system text (role, rules, ctx.profile.system_text(), few-shot examples) goes in system_stable; retrieved documents and the question go in the user message. Never put timestamps/UUIDs/request ids in stable blocks. Never pass temperature/top_p/top_k or budget_tokens; never append date suffixes to model IDs. Use output_schema (sanitize_schema(PydanticModel.model_json_schema())) for every machine-read output and validate with model_validate.
