- Specification: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section "${m.section}" lists the REQUIRED modules, classes, plan schema, defaults and direct API. Implement everything listed there; you may add more.
- Component name for ComponentSpec.name and registry: "${m.pkg}". Class name: ${m.cls}. Config class: ${m.cls.replace('Model', 'Config')}. Plan class as named in the spec.
- Research dossiers to ground design decisions, defaults and README citations: ${research}. Read them (they are JSON: papers with key_contribution/design_implication, techniques with default_parameters, architecture_recommendations, pitfalls, evaluation_metrics, engineering_adaptation_notes, composition_notes). Where a dossier's literature-backed default differs from the spec's suggested default, prefer the literature and document why.

${STANDARDS}

PROCESS
1. Read the core sources and the spec; sketch the module layout and the plan schema.
2. Write config.py, plan.py (schema + HeuristicPlanner), prompts.py (versioned PromptTemplates), the technique modules, model.py, evaluation.py, cli.py, __init__.py (export classes; call pipeline_core.register on the model class).
3. Write tests; run them; iterate until green. Run the CLI offline and both examples.
4. Write the README last so it matches the code exactly.
5. Return the structured report. In "public_api" list every public class/function another model or an orchestrator would call, with its signature. In "deviations" list anything from the spec you changed or could not implement and why.`
}

function reviewPrompt(m, report) {
  return `You are an adversarial senior reviewer. Your job is to find real defects in the "${m.pkg}" package, not to praise it. Assume there are bugs until you have evidence otherwise.

${ENV}

Package under review: ${m.folder}/ (package ${m.pkg}, class ${m.cls}). Specification: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md (sections 2, 3, 5, 6 and "${m.section}"). Shared core: common/pipeline_core/*.py.

Implementer's report (claims to verify, not to trust):
${JSON.stringify(report, null, 1)}

Checklist - do each and record evidence:
1. Run: cd "${REPO}" && python -m pytest ${m.folder}/tests -q . Record pass/fail counts. Then run the CLI offline and both examples; record any exception.
2. Spec compliance: for every module/class/function named in the spec section, confirm it exists with the specified behaviour. List each missing or renamed item as a finding.
3. Core API misuse: read model.py and every module that touches the LLM. Verify: calls go through ctx.llm_call where a ctx exists; stable/volatile prompt split is respected (no timestamps/uuids/request-specific text in system_stable); output_schema used for machine-read outputs and validated; no temperature/top_p/top_k/budget_tokens; no date-suffixed model IDs; plan() works offline via heuristics and online via a structured call; statuses and confidence set per section 3.1 (NEEDS_REVIEW below ctx.profile.min_confidence_to_accept or constraints.min_confidence); nested component usage charged via ctx.charge.
4. Correctness of pure logic: read the technique modules and look for off-by-one errors, wrong formulas (e.g. BM25 idf, RRF 1/(k+rank) with 1-based rank, min-max normalisation with equal scores, nDCG discount, exponential backoff caps, LRU eviction order, cycle detection, topological ordering, threshold comparisons), async misuse (blocking calls, un-awaited coroutines, unbounded gather), exception swallowing, mutable default arguments, and non-deterministic iteration over sets/dicts feeding prompts or cache keys.
5. Domain adaptation: confirm behaviour actually changes with ctx.profile (weights, rules, thresholds), not just text.
6. README vs code: every class, function, config field, default value and CLI flag mentioned in README must exist with that exact name and default. Every citation must appear in docs/research/${m.key}.draft.json (match on title). List mismatches.
7. Test quality: are the LLM-planned path, failure paths and domain adaptation actually tested? Are tests deterministic (no real network, no time.sleep > 0.1 s)?

Write concrete findings with file path, line number, what is wrong, why it matters, and the exact fix. Severity: critical = wrong results/crash/spec violation on the main path; major = incorrect edge behaviour, missing required feature, README lies; minor = style, naming, small doc gaps. Do not modify any files.`
}

function fixPrompt(m, review) {
  return `You are the engineer who owns the "${m.pkg}" package (${m.folder}/). An adversarial review produced the findings below. Fix every critical and major finding and as many minor ones as are cheap. If a finding is wrong, explain why in "skipped" with evidence.

${ENV}

Rules: follow docs/ARCHITECTURE.md and common/pipeline_core/*.py exactly; do not change files outside ${m.folder}/; keep the README in sync with any code change (and vice versa); after fixing, run cd "${REPO}" && python -m pytest ${m.folder}/tests -q and the offline CLI and both examples; all must pass. Add a regression test for every critical/major fix.

REVIEW FINDINGS:
${JSON.stringify(review, null, 1)}`
}

const REPORT_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    model: { type: 'string' },
    files: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    tests_passed: { type: 'integer' },
    tests_failed: { type: 'integer' },
    cli_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    examples_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    public_api: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' }, description: 'Public classes/functions with signatures that other models or orchestrators call' },
    config_defaults: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' }, description: 'field=default (source) for each config field' },
    deviations: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    core_change_requests: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    notes: { type: 'string' },
  },
  required: ['model', 'files', 'tests_passed', 'tests_failed', 'cli_ok', 'examples_ok', 'public_api', 'config_defaults', 'deviations', 'core_change_requests', 'notes'],
}

const REVIEW_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    tests_passed: { type: 'integer' },
    tests_failed: { type: 'integer' },
    cli_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    examples_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    findings: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['critical', 'major', 'minor'] },
          file: { type: 'string' },
          line: { type: 'integer' },
          summary: { type: 'string' },
          why_it_matters: { type: 'string' },
          fix: { type: 'string' },
        },
        required: ['severity', 'file', 'line', 'summary', 'why_it_matters', 'fix'],
      },
    },
    readme_mismatches: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    spec_gaps: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    uncited_or_invented_citations: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
  required: ['tests_passed', 'tests_failed', 'cli_ok', 'examples_ok', 'findings', 'readme_mismatches', 'spec_gaps', 'uncited_or_invented_citations'],
}

const FIX_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    fixed: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    skipped: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    tests_passed: { type: 'integer' },
    tests_failed: { type: 'integer' },
    cli_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    examples_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    public_api: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' }, description: 'Final public API with signatures after fixes' },
    notes: { type: 'string' },
  },
  required: ['fixed', 'skipped', 'tests_passed', 'tests_failed', 'cli_ok', 'examples_ok', 'public_api', 'notes'],
}

const INTEGRATION_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    files: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    tests_passed: { type: 'integer' },
    tests_failed: { type: 'integer' },
    example_ran_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    api_issues: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' }, description: 'Cross-package API frictions found while wiring, with file and suggested change' },
    pipeline_description: { type: 'string', description: 'Precise description of the wiring and data flow for the main README' },
    notes: { type: 'string' },
  },
  required: ['files', 'tests_passed', 'tests_failed', 'example_ran_ok', 'api_issues', 'pipeline_description', 'notes'],
}

log(`Implementing ${MODELS.length} model packages in parallel, each followed by review and fix`)

const results = await pipeline(
  MODELS,
  m => agent(implementPrompt(m), { label: `implement:${m.pkg}`, phase: 'Implement', schema: REPORT_SCHEMA, effort: 'high' }),
  async (report, m) => {
    if (!report) { log(`${m.pkg}: implementer returned nothing`); return null }
    log(`${m.pkg}: implemented, tests ${report.tests_passed} passed / ${report.tests_failed} failed; reviewing`)
    const review = await agent(reviewPrompt(m, report), { label: `review:${m.pkg}`, phase: 'Review', schema: REVIEW_SCHEMA, effort: 'high' })
    return { report, review }
  },
  async (prev, m) => {
    if (!prev) return null
    const { report, review } = prev
    if (!review) { log(`${m.pkg}: review failed; skipping fix`); return { model: m, report, review: null, fix: null } }
